{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our single completed experiment (config_003) achieved 61.9% accuracy using PCA-2000 for RNA, ResNet50 for image, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion in a multimodal multiprofile setting. The biggest uncertainty is whether the linear PCA representation is sufficient for the RNA modality or whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) would capture more biologically relevant structure and improve accuracy. Question tested: config_002 is a clean single-variable ablation of config_003—only the RNA encoder changes from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200, holding all other settings (multimodal, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat) constant. This isolates the contribution of the RNA representation. Why this is the best next experiment: With 8 experiments remaining, resolving whether the RNA encoder is a bottleneck is fundamental—if scvi_n200 helps, it unlocks a large family of scvi-based configurations for later exploitation; if it does not, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can focus budget on the image encoder, aggregation, and fusion dimensions. Expected relative cost: comparable to config_003 (~35–40 GPU hours), since scvi_n200 inference is a single forward pass through a pre-trained VAE encoder, only marginally more expensive than a PCA projection, while the rest of the pipeline (ResNet50, avgpool, concat, multiprofile) is unchanged."
}

